      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "I second this.\n\nHTC's manufacturing quality is marginal at best. It's only a matter of time before the rubber pads underneath the track-pad come loose. At that point continuing to use the controllers can actually permanently damage the microswitches. The trackpads on the steam controllers are so, so much higher quality. I don't know why HTC had to be the ones to make the controllers.\n\nFor anyone else who has broken touchpads, stop using them immediately and either RMA them (good luck with that, HTC will fight you tooth and nail to not have to honor their warranty) or fix them according to this guide: https://www.reddit.com/r/Vive/comments/4lkkh1/guide_how_to_fix_your_stuck_trackpad_in_the_vive/",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
