  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-09-27T06:42:26.773Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Please add an option for Vive users to swap the controls so that just touching the touch pads moves the player and clicking down the pads does the hand gestures.\n\nThe vive wands have significant issues with the durability of the buttons underneath the trackpads. It would be nice if I didn't need to constantly click the pads just to move. Just from about 30 hrs in VRChat, I've already significantly worn out the trackpad click buttons on my left controller.\n\nAlso, the current setup prevents vive users from fully using objects enabled by hand gesture override animations. While standing still, everyone can use hand gesture override animations to add/remove objects from their avatar. However, for Vive users the objects get automatically disabled when we move. In order to click the pads to move one must first touch the pads, which automatically changes the hand gesture and disables the objects. Oculus users can freely move without disabling the objects however.",
